/// getApiDoc() text for the property canister (see backend/shared/ApiDoc.mo).
import Shared "../shared/ApiDoc";

module {
  public func text() : Text {
    "# HomeGentic property canister\n\n" #
    "Holds the homes a user has registered, who may act on each one, and the rooms and fixtures inside it. Most other canisters take a `propertyId` from here.\n\n" #
    "## Reading\n" #
    "- `getMyProperties()` (query): the caller's own properties. Start here to get `propertyId`s.\n" #
    "- `getMyManagedProperties()` (query): properties the caller manages for someone else, with their role.\n" #
    "- `getProperty(id)` (query): one property, if the caller owns or manages it.\n" #
    "- `getRoomsByProperty(propertyId)` / `getRoom(id)` (query): rooms and the fixtures in them (appliances, model numbers, install dates).\n" #
    "- `getOwnershipHistory(propertyId)` (query): past owner transfers.\n" #
    "- `getInsurancePolicy(propertyId)` (query): the home insurance policy details the household saved (carrier, policy number, renewal date as YYYY-MM-DD, Coverage A and hurricane deductible), or null. HomeGentic doesn't check them with the insurer.\n" #
    "- `getInsuranceClaims(propertyId)` (query): the household's records of insurance claims on the home, newest date of loss first, each with its dated log (`log`: date, note). These are the household's own notes; HomeGentic doesn't file or track anything with the insurer.\n" #
    "- `getInventory(propertyId)` (query): the household's list of what's in the home (name, category, quantity, value in cents, purchase date, serial number, notes, and the room it's in, if any), for an insurance claim. Only the household can read it.\n" #
    "- `getHouseGuide(propertyId)` (query): the house guide the household wrote for sitters and guests (Wi-Fi name and password, alarm notes, trash and recycling days, where the water, gas and electrical shutoffs are, contacts, notes, and ids of photos shown with it), or null. Passwords and alarm codes are stored exactly as the household typed them.\n" #
    "- `listHouseGuideLinks(propertyId)` (query): the home's guide links (token, name, created, expires, revoked), newest first; older expired or turned-off links are cleared as new ones are made. Only callers with write access to the home see them.\n" #
    "- `getSharedHouseGuide(token)` (query): what a guide link shows: the guide and the home's street address. Anyone holding the token can read it until it expires or is revoked; unknown, revoked and expired links all return `#NotFound`.\n" #
    "- `guideSharesPhoto(token, propertyId, photoId)` (query): for HomeGentic's photo canister; true when the link is live for that home and its guide shows that photo.\n" #
    "- `getArchitecturalReviews(propertyId)` (query): the household's log of architectural review requests to the HOA or condo association (project, details, submitted date, status, decision date, conditions, approval letter document id, job id), newest first.\n" #
    "- `getSpecialAssessments(propertyId)` (query): special assessments the association levied on the home (title, amount in cents, due date, paid date or empty, notes, document id), latest due date first.\n" #
    "- `getCondoAssociationRecord(propertyId)` (query): for a condo, what the owner entered about the association's milestone inspection and structural reserve study (dates as YYYY-MM-DD or empty, document ids, notes), or null. HomeGentic doesn't check it with the association and it says nothing about whether a building is safe.\n" #
    "- `getPulseInsurance(owner)` (query): only for HomeGentic's notification relay, which emails the renewal reminder. Any other caller gets `#NotAuthorized`.\n\n" #
    "## Changing\n" #
    "- `registerProperty(args)`: adds a home. `state` is a 2-letter code, `zipCode` 5 digits or ZIP+4, `squareFeet` 1 to 100,000. Free accounts can register 1 property and Pro accounts 20. Registering an address you already own returns that home unchanged and creates nothing. If another user has verified that address, the call is refused with `#DuplicateAddress`. If another user has claimed it without verifying, `#AddressConflict` gives the end of a 7-day window for resolving it.\n" #
    "- `submitVerification(propertyId, method, documentHash, nameOnDoc)`: asks HomeGentic to verify ownership from a document the user uploaded in the web app. It moves the property to `#PendingReview`. A HomeGentic administrator approves it.\n" #
    "- `createRoom`, `updateRoom`, `deleteRoom`, `addFixture`, `updateFixture`, `removeFixture`: edit rooms and fixtures. `deleteRoom` and `removeFixture` can't be undone.\n" #
    "- `setInsurancePolicy(propertyId, policy)`: saves the home's insurance policy details, or clears them with null. Needs write access to the home (owner, co-owner or manager). `carrier` is required (up to 100 characters), `policyNumber` up to 60, `renewalDate` a real date written YYYY-MM-DD. `coverageACents` and a dollar hurricane deductible are in cents; a percent hurricane deductible is a whole percent of Coverage A, 1 to 25. This only records what the policy says: it doesn't contact the insurer or change the policy. The details are removed when the home is transferred to a new owner.\n" #
    "- `createInsuranceClaim(propertyId, input)` / `updateInsuranceClaim(claimId, input)`: start or edit a claim record: `title` (required, up to 100 characters), `dateOfLoss` (YYYY-MM-DD), `cause`, `description`, `claimNumber`, `adjusterName`, `adjusterContact`, `status` (`#Open` or `#Closed`). Needs write access to the home; at most 50 claims per home. This doesn't file a claim or contact the insurer.\n" #
    "- `addInsuranceClaimLog(claimId, date, note)`: adds a dated line to the claim's log (a call, a visit, a letter). Entries can't be edited or removed one by one.\n" #
    "- `deleteInsuranceClaim(claimId)`: deletes a claim record and its log. It can't be undone. Claim records are also removed when the home is transferred.\n" #
    "- `inviteManager(...)` creates an invite link that gives another person access to the property. `removeManager` and `updateManagerRole` change that access.\n" #
    "- `addInventoryItem(propertyId, input)` / `updateInventoryItem(itemId, input)`: add or edit an item in the home's contents inventory: `name` (required, up to 100 characters), `category` (up to 40), `quantity` 1 to 999, `valueCents` (optional, up to $100,000,000), `purchaseDate` (empty, or YYYY-MM-DD from 1900 on), `serialNumber`, `notes`, and `roomId` (a room on this home, or none). Needs write access to the home; at most 500 items per home. This only records what the household enters; HomeGentic doesn't appraise anything or send it to an insurer.\n" #
    "- `deleteInventoryItem(itemId)`: deletes an inventory item. It can't be undone. The inventory is also removed when the home is transferred.\n" #
    "- `setHouseGuide(propertyId, guide)`: saves the home's house guide, or clears it with null, which also ends every link to it. Needs write access to the home. Every field is optional but the guide can't be empty; up to 10 contacts and 6 photo ids. The guide and its links are removed when the home is transferred to a new owner.\n" #
    "- `createHouseGuideLink(propertyId, name, expiryDays)`: creates a link that shows the guide, including any Wi-Fi password and alarm code in it, and the home's street address to anyone who has it, for 1 to 90 days. Needs write access and a saved guide; at most 10 live links per home.\n" #
    "- `revokeHouseGuideLink(token)`: ends a guide link at once. It can't be turned back on; create a new link instead.\n" #
    "- `addArchitecturalReview(propertyId, input)` / `updateArchitecturalReview(reviewId, input)`: log or edit an architectural review request: `project` (required, up to 120 characters), `details`, `submittedDate` and `decisionDate` (YYYY-MM-DD or empty), `status` (`#Planned`, `#Submitted`, `#Approved`, `#ApprovedWithConditions`, `#Denied`, `#Withdrawn`), `conditions`, `approvalDocId`, `jobId`. A submitted request needs its submitted date and a decision needs its decision date. Needs write access; at most 100 per home. Nothing is sent to the association.\n" #
    "- `addSpecialAssessment(propertyId, input)` / `updateSpecialAssessment(assessmentId, input)`: record or edit a special assessment: `title` (required), `amountCents` (more than 0, up to $100,000,000), `dueDate` (YYYY-MM-DD), `paidDate` (YYYY-MM-DD or empty while unpaid), `notes`, `documentId`. Needs write access; at most 100 per home. This doesn't pay anything.\n" #
    "- `deleteArchitecturalReview(reviewId)` / `deleteSpecialAssessment(assessmentId)`: delete a record. It can't be undone. Review requests, assessments and the condo record stay with the home when it is transferred.\n" #
    "- `setCondoAssociationRecord(propertyId, record)`: saves the condo association's milestone inspection and reserve study dates, document ids and notes as the owner knows them, or clears them with null. Condo homes only; needs write access.\n" #
    "- Ownership transfers (`initiateTransfer`, `claimTransfer`, `cancelTransfer`) hand the home and its record to a new owner. A transfer can't be reversed once claimed.\n\n" #
    Shared.common()
  };
};
